                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. White to Mr. Foster.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-12-10"><hi rendition="#italic">December 10, 1892</hi></date>.
                        (Received December 21.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 865.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your instruction No. 951 of
                    the 5th ultimo, and to my dispatch No. 841 of November 21, I have the honor to
                    acquaint you that Lord Rosebery informed me during a recent interview which I
                    had with his lordship in reference to other matters, that orders have been
                    circulated by the admiralty to commanders of Her Majesty’s ships, directing them
                    to recognize in the usual manner the United States consular agent in the Gilbert
                    Islands.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry White.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
